{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44129778",
      "title": "Creating & Using Async Validators",
      "lectureOrder": 256,
      "videoOrder": 244,
      "sourceHash": "3d3b38ea7213162ded79db70584d362b1930cd6d8d137af737fdfb57bd4c6047",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 3.78,
          "en": "Now besides regular validator functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.78,
          "end": 7.5,
          "en": "you can also register async validators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.5,
          "end": 12.45,
          "en": "and an async validator is in the end also just a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.45,
          "end": 16.14,
          "en": "that gets a control as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.14,
          "end": 20.61,
          "en": "but it's then a function that must return an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.61,
          "end": 22.98,
          "en": "And this allows you to do things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.98,
          "end": 26.82,
          "en": "like send an HTTP request to a backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.82,
          "end": 28.98,
          "en": "to check whether an email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.98,
          "end": 32.73,
          "en": "already was registered there or not, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.73,
          "end": 35.79,
          "en": "In the end, the observable should then yield null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.79,
          "end": 38.7,
          "en": "if the input is considered valid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.7,
          "end": 41.88,
          "en": "or an error object as we did it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.88,
          "end": 45.063,
          "en": "if it's considered invalid, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.99,
          "end": 47.73,
          "en": "So to quickly show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.73,
          "end": 51.84,
          "en": "how you could create such an async validator function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.84,
          "end": 53.31,
          "en": "I'll add one here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.31,
          "end": 56.34,
          "en": "and it'll just be a dummy validator function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.34,
          "end": 58.02,
          "en": "That's not actually useful here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.02,
          "end": 61.5,
          "en": "but that shows you how you would create one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.5,
          "end": 63.87,
          "en": "because here I'll just add one that checks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.87,
          "end": 68.37,
          "en": "if email is unique,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.37,
          "end": 70.62,
          "en": "and for that I'll get my control,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.62,
          "end": 73.62,
          "en": "which is of type abstract control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.62,
          "end": 78.62,
          "en": "And I'll then check if if control.value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.28,
          "end": 85.28,
          "en": "is equal to test@example.com, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.13,
          "end": 87.18,
          "en": "If that's the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.18,
          "end": 89.67,
          "en": "I consider the email to not be unique",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.67,
          "end": 93.3,
          "en": "because let's say that's already a registered email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.3,
          "end": 94.62,
          "en": "Though of course in reality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.62,
          "end": 96.93,
          "en": "you would not hard code this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.93,
          "end": 98.72999999999999,
          "en": "but instead as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.72999999999999,
          "end": 102.6,
          "en": "send an HTTP request to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.6,
          "end": 105.21000000000001,
          "en": "But here for demo purposes, I'll hardcode it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.21000000000001,
          "end": 107.1,
          "en": "and if this condition is met,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.1,
          "end": 110.67,
          "en": "the input is therefore considered to be invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.67,
          "end": 112.68,
          "en": "So here I would return my object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.68,
          "end": 114.72,
          "en": "that contains the error code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.72,
          "end": 118.47,
          "en": "Or to be precise, I would return an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.47,
          "end": 121.413,
          "en": "that in the end emits that object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.09,
          "end": 126.63,
          "en": "Now to be in line with the structure of my first validator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.63,
          "end": 130.56,
          "en": "to make things not more confusing than necessary,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.56,
          "end": 133.26,
          "en": "I'll actually check for the opposite here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.26,
          "end": 135.6,
          "en": "so that here I want to return null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.6,
          "end": 138.18,
          "en": "but still we don't return null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.18,
          "end": 141.993,
          "en": "Instead we return an observable that emits null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.19,
          "end": 146.46,
          "en": "We can do this by using the of function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.46,
          "end": 149.64,
          "en": "which can be imported from RXJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.64,
          "end": 152.94,
          "en": "because of produces an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.94,
          "end": 155.46,
          "en": "that instantly emits a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.46,
          "end": 157.563,
          "en": "in this case null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.51,
          "end": 161.34,
          "en": "And if we make it past this if check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.34,
          "end": 163.23,
          "en": "I know that I have an invalid value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.23,
          "end": 166.05,
          "en": "So then I'll return an observable with help of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.05,
          "end": 170.16,
          "en": "of that will emit such an error object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.16,
          "end": 174.66,
          "en": "And here I'll give this an error key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.66,
          "end": 176.94299999999998,
          "en": "of not unique and set this to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.99,
          "end": 181.29,
          "en": "And this is now an async validator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.29,
          "end": 185.43,
          "en": "We can now use this email is unique function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 185.43,
          "end": 188.58,
          "en": "and register this as an async validator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 188.58,
          "end": 190.77,
          "en": "though not here for the password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.77,
          "end": 193.38,
          "en": "but instead here for the email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.38,
          "end": 195.54,
          "en": "With that, if I saved it all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.54,
          "end": 198.15,
          "en": "and I go back, you'll see that if I enter an email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.15,
          "end": 200.91,
          "en": "that's equal to test@example.com,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 200.91,
          "end": 204.93,
          "en": "I get an error even though it's a valid email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 204.93,
          "end": 207.15,
          "en": "because it's now not unique",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 207.15,
          "end": 211.413,
          "en": "according to this dummy demo async validator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 212.31,
          "end": 215.91,
          "en": "If I enter anything but test@example.com,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.91,
          "end": 219.03,
          "en": "for example test2@example.com,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 219.03,
          "end": 221.19,
          "en": "the error goes away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 221.19,
          "end": 222.84,
          "en": "and that's therefore how you can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 222.84,
          "end": 224.94,
          "en": "set up async validators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 224.94,
          "end": 226.71,
          "en": "Here it's a simple example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.71,
          "end": 228.48,
          "en": "but of course you can perform",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 228.48,
          "end": 232.323,
          "en": "any asynchronous logic you want to perform in there.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
